---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="SDK"
  description="The Lumen plugin SDK: interfaces, event bus, and model registry."
  lang="en"
  altHref="/sdk/"
>
  <div class="hero">
    <h1>SDK</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Lumen is built around a public plugin SDK: anyone can write a new module following the same
      interfaces the official modules use.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>Where the contracts live</h2>
    <p>
      The plugin contract (<code>LumenPlugin</code>), the event bus (<code>LumenEventBus</code>),
      and the model registry (<code>ModelRegistry</code>) are defined in
      <a href="https://github.com/lumen-assistive/lumen-sdk">lumen-sdk</a> and implemented in
      <a href="https://github.com/lumen-assistive/lumen-core">lumen-core</a>. Full documentation for
      both lives directly in their own repositories, not duplicated here.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Building a plugin</h2>
    <p>
      Every Lumen module lives in a single repository,
      <a href="https://github.com/lumen-assistive/lumen-plugins">lumen-plugins</a>, and a new module
      is proposed as a pull request. The full, step-by-step guide is in the documentation section:
    </p>
    <p>
      <a class="button primary" href="/docs/contributing/plugins/">Guide to building a plugin</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Full documentation</h2>
    <p>
      Architecture, API reference, and contributor guides are all in the
      <a href="/docs/">documentation</a> section.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
